==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|tender|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛn.dɚ.li/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛn.də.li/|a=RP}}
* {{hyph|en|ten|der|ly}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-tenderly.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[tender]] manner; [[gently]]; [[sweetly]].
#* {{RQ:Cleland Fanny Hill|passage=and the hour striking at which I was oblig'd to dispatch my young man, I '''tenderly''' advised him of the necessity there was for parting}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Victoria J. Hyla|title=Running in the Mists|series=Hearts Drawn Wyld Trilogy|seriesvolume=2|location=Bloomington, Ind.|publisher=w:AuthorHouse|year=2013|page=300|isbn=978-1-4772-9662-2|passage=After a moment of comfortable silence, with Ben '''tenderly''' rubbing his thumb gently over the back of her hand, he asked, “So what do you want to do now that you’re all stuffed full of waffley goodness?”}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2019|artist=w:Clairo|title={{w|Immunity (Clairo album)|Sinking}}|passage=Outside is getting colder<br/>Why does it feel like I'm older than I asked to be?<br/>But when you say my name<br/>It all falls away so '''tenderly'''}}

